{"slug": "arroz-con-maiz-y-crema-cheesy-rice-casserole-with-corn", "nyt_id": 1024693, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1024693-arroz-con-maiz-y-crema-cheesy-rice-casserole-with-corn", "name": "Arroz con Maiz y Crema (Cheesy Rice Casserole With Corn)", "author": "Christina Morales", "description": "Sandra A. Gutierrez, the author of “Latinísimo: Home Recipes from the 21 Countries of Latin America” (Knopf, 2023), was born in Philadelphia and raised by her Guatemalan parents in their home country. This recipe, a classic from Guatemala City where she lived, has been made since the 1950s, when mayonnaise started gaining popularity in Latin America as it became available in grocery stores. Ms. Gutierrez says the dish is typically enjoyed alongside buffet dinners with roast chicken or beef tenderloin. A satisfyingly easy side dish that is rich, cheesy and tangy, this casserole can be prepared and assembled in advance, or easily halved for a smaller crowd. Christina Morales", "servings": {"text": "8 to 12 servings", "min": 8, "max": 12, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 10, "cook_minutes": 40, "total_minutes": 50, "raw": {"prep": "PT10M", "cook": "PT40M", "total": "PT50M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "Butter, as needed for greasing", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "butter", "preparation": "as needed for greasing", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "6 (lightly packed) cups/800 grams cooked white rice (preferably medium- or long-grain)", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "/800 grams cooked white rice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 cups fresh corn kernels (or frozen, thawed)", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "fresh corn kernels (or frozen", "preparation": "thawed)", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 ½ cups/340 grams sour cream", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "/340 grams sour cream", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 cup/225 grams mayonnaise", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "/225 grams mayonnaise", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 cup finely grated Cotija, queso seco or Parmesan", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "finely grated cotija", "preparation": "queso seco or Parmesan", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 cup finely chopped fresh parsley leaves and tender stems", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "finely chopped fresh parsley leaves and tender stems", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "½ cup finely chopped scallions", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "finely chopped scallions", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 large drained, roasted red bell peppers (about 6 ounces), thinly sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "large drained", "preparation": "roasted red bell peppers (about 6 ounces), thinly sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 teaspoon fine sea salt", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "fine sea salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "¼ teaspoon freshly ground black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "tsp", "item": "freshly ground black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "1 ½ cups/115 grams shredded Chihuahua, Monterey Jack or other melting cheese", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "/115 grams shredded chihuahua", "preparation": "Monterey Jack or other melting cheese", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Heat the oven to 350 degrees. Butter a 9-by-13-inch baking dish."}, {"position": 2, "text": "In a large bowl, combine the rice, corn, sour cream, mayonnaise, Cotija, parsley, scallions, roasted red pepper, salt and pepper. Spread the mixture into the prepared baking dish, sprinkle with the shredded cheese and bake until bubbly, about 30 minutes."}, {"position": 3, "text": "If you’d like additional color on your casserole, broil the casserole a few inches away from your broiler heat source until golden in spots, about 3 minutes. Let cool a few minutes, then serve hot."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 618.7, "protein_g": 11.6, "carbohydrates_g": 63.1, "fat_g": 35.7, "saturated_fat_g": 12.6, "unsaturated_fat_g": 11.3, "trans_fat_g": 0.3, "cholesterol_mg": 61.5, "sodium_mg": 622.4, "fiber_g": 1.8, "sugar_g": 3.1, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["central-american"], "diet": [], "course": ["casseroles-dinner-grains-and-rice-main-course-side-dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["corn", "cotija", "easy", "great-leftovers", "make-ahead", "mayonnaise", "rice", "sour-cream", "vegetarian-thanksgiving", "weeknight"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2023/10/10/multimedia/10LATINISIMOrex2-rice-gvwf/10LATINISIMOrex2-rice-gvwf-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg", "alt": "Since the 1950s, home cooks in Guatemala City have made cheesy rice casserole with corn and mayonnaise, which became popular throughout Latin America as it became available in grocery stores.", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2023/10/10/multimedia/10LATINISIMOrex2-rice-gvwf/10LATINISIMOrex2-rice-gvwf-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "Since the 1950s, home cooks in Guatemala City have made cheesy rice casserole with corn and mayonnaise, which became popular throughout Latin America as it became available in grocery stores.", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2023/10/10/multimedia/10LATINISIMOrex2-rice-gvwf/10LATINISIMOrex2-rice-gvwf-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg", "alt": "Since the 1950s, home cooks in Guatemala City have made cheesy rice casserole with corn and mayonnaise, which became popular throughout Latin America as it 